CAT = "bcgArrest"; SEG = "ARR"
Q = [
("A guard arrests a shoplifter. The store manager says to let him go once he pays. Under section 494(3), the guard must:",
 "Deliver him to police", ["Release him", "Release him with a ban notice", "Hold him until the owner decides"],
 "Section 494(3) says anyone other than a peace officer who arrests without warrant shall forthwith deliver the person to a peace officer. The manager cannot override that duty."),
("Section 494(4) says a person authorized to arrest under section 494 is authorized by law for the purposes of:",
 "Section 25", ["Section 34", "Section 35", "Section 129"],
 "Section 494(4) links a lawful private arrest to section 25, which justifies doing what you are authorized to do, with necessary force, when acting on reasonable grounds."),
("A thief returns to the mall a week after the theft, and police are already on scene. Arresting him yourself under section 494(2) is:",
 "Not justified, police can act", ["Justified, it's your client's site", "Justified within 30 days", "Justified with owner consent"],
 "Section 494(2)(b) allows an arrest after the fact only within a reasonable time and only if it is not feasible for a peace officer to make the arrest."),
("Section 494(1)(b) covers a person who committed a criminal offence and is fleeing from and freshly pursued by:",
 "Those with power to arrest", ["The victim's friends only", "A crowd of bystanders", "Store staff only"],
 "The pursuit must be by persons who have lawful authority to arrest that person. You must also believe on reasonable grounds that the person committed a criminal offence."),
("As the owner's agent, your arrest power under section 494(2) covers criminal offences committed:",
 "On or about that property", ["Anywhere in the city", "Only inside buildings", "Only with violence"],
 "Section 494(2) applies to a person found committing a criminal offence on or in relation to the property the owner, possessor or their agent protects."),
("Your arrest power under section 494(2) depends on being:",
 "Acting for the owner", ["Licensed", "Trained in restraints", "Appointed by the police"],
 "Section 494(2) applies to the owner, a person in lawful possession of property, or a person they authorize. A guard posted by the client is authorized."),
("You arrest someone but forget to tell them why. Under section 29(3) this:",
 "Doesn't alone cost you protection", ["Makes the arrest void", "Means you must release them", "Is an offence by itself"],
 "Section 29(2) requires notice of the reason where feasible, but section 29(3) says failing to give it does not of itself deprive the arrester of protection from criminal responsibility."),
("A clerk tells you a customer stole earlier, but you saw nothing yourself. Arresting the customer under section 494(2) is:",
 "Not justified, you didn't find it", ["Justified, the clerk saw it", "Justified if the clerk signs a note", "Justified within 24 hours"],
 "Section 494(2) requires that you find the person committing the offence. Pass the clerk's information to police and record it."),
("Under BC's Trespass Act, who may arrest a trespasser without warrant?",
 "A peace officer", ["A licensed security guard", "The occupier", "Any authorized person"],
 "Section 7 of the Trespass Act gives the arrest power to peace officers only. A guard can direct a trespasser to leave and ask for a name and address, then call police."),
("Besides police, which officer is a peace officer for arrests under BC's Trespass Act?",
 "A conservation officer", ["A licensed security guard", "A liquor inspector", "A municipal bylaw officer"],
 "Section 7(1) defines peace officer for the section to include conservation officers under the Environmental Management Act."),
("Under the Trespass Act, a peace officer may arrest a trespasser who has already left the premises if the person:",
 "Won't give name and address", ["Swore at the guard", "Came back within a week", "Has no photo ID"],
 "Section 7(3) allows the arrest of someone who has recently left if they refuse to give their name and address, or the officer believes the details given are false."),
("You see someone commit an indictable offence on the public street outside your site. Section 494(1)(a):",
 "Still applies to anyone", ["Doesn't apply off site", "Applies only to police", "Applies only if licensed"],
 "Section 494(1)(a) lets any one arrest a person found committing an indictable offence. It is not tied to property, unlike section 494(2)."),
("You saw a theft in the store, but the thief left before you could act. Under section 494(2)(b), a later arrest must be within:",
 "A reasonable time", ["One hour", "Twenty-four hours", "The same shift"],
 "Section 494(2)(b) allows an arrest within a reasonable time after the offence when it is not feasible for a peace officer to make it. No fixed number of hours is set."),
("On a public road away from your site you see a person commit a minor summary offence. Under section 494 you:",
 "Have no arrest power", ["May arrest under 494(1)(a)", "May arrest as owner's agent", "May arrest if they walk off"],
 "Section 494(1)(a) needs an indictable offence, and section 494(2) needs an offence on or in relation to the property you protect. Neither applies."),
("An arrest by a security guard under section 494 is made:",
 "Without a warrant", ["With a warrant", "With a police permit", "With registrar approval"],
 "Section 494 is headed \"Arrest without warrant\". A guard never obtains warrants."),
("Under section 494(1)(b), your belief that the fleeing person committed an offence must rest on:",
 "Reasonable grounds", ["A strong hunch", "A rumour from staff", "Proof beyond doubt"],
 "The section requires a belief on reasonable grounds. Proof beyond a reasonable doubt is the standard at trial, not for an arrest."),
("Section 494(1)(b) covers a fleeing person who has committed:",
 "Any criminal offence", ["Only an indictable offence", "Only a property offence", "Only a provincial offence"],
 "Paragraph (b) uses the words \"a criminal offence\", while paragraph (a) is limited to indictable offences found being committed."),
("You arrest a person at 2 a.m. Your shift ends at 6 a.m. You should:",
 "Call police right away", ["Hold him till 6 a.m.", "Release him at shift end", "Drive him to the station"],
 "Section 494(3) requires delivery to a peace officer forthwith. Policy also bars using a patrol vehicle to hold or transport an arrested person."),
("A calm person refuses your direction to leave a mall and stays put. Your power to arrest them is:",
 "None; call the police", ["Section 494(2) as agent", "Section 7 of the Trespass Act", "Section 8 of the Security Services Act"],
 "Refusing to leave is an offence under the Trespass Act, which is provincial, not a criminal offence for section 494(2). Only a peace officer may arrest under section 7 of the Trespass Act."),
("Under the Trespass Act, a police officer may arrest someone found on premises when the officer believes on reasonable and probable grounds the person:",
 "Is trespassing there", ["Is unknown to the staff", "Looks out of place", "Is a stranger"],
 "Section 7(2) allows a peace officer to arrest without warrant a person found on premises who is committing an offence under section 2."),
("Your client tells you to arrest anyone who looks suspicious. Under section 494 you may arrest:",
 "Only as the Code allows", ["Anyone the client names", "Anyone refusing a search", "Anyone without a receipt"],
 "A client cannot add arrest powers. You may arrest only when section 494 applies, for example when you find someone committing an offence on the property."),
("A customer who has not been seen stealing refuses to let you search her bag. You:",
 "Can't force a search", ["May arrest her", "May search it anyway", "May hold her for police"],
 "No law gives a guard a general power to search a person or their bag. Refusing a search is not an offence and gives no ground for arrest."),
("You see a man spray-paint your client's wall and you stop him on the spot. Your power is section 494(2) because:",
 "You found him committing it", ["He is on enclosed land", "You hold a guard licence", "The client has insurance"],
 "Section 494(2)(a) applies when the owner's agent finds someone committing a criminal offence on or in relation to the property and arrests at that time. Mischief to property is such an offence."),
("A business that rents its store, rather than owning the building, is under section 494(2):",
 "A person in lawful possession", ["Unable to authorize a guard", "Only a licensed occupant", "Covered only with the landlord's consent"],
 "Section 494(2) covers the owner or a person in lawful possession of property, and anyone either of them authorizes. A tenant running a store is in lawful possession."),
]
